From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:49:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 081/207] lanes: a window feeding a forced result takes the
 last fed row's drafts past it

A lone stream's round that feeds a runner's (or tool's) owned result used to
carry no drafts: the depth rule gave 0 while forced tokens were queued, and a
forced window held only the forced tokens. Now, when the window takes the
whole forced tail with room left, it appends the drafts the previous round
made from its last fed row, past the forced positions (the trigger round's
drafts for a short result; a forced round drafts depth + tail for a longer
one). Forced rows always land; the drafts after them are verified like any
draft, so greedy and sampled replies are unchanged.

The trigger round already keeps every draft it accepted before the trigger;
the fire replay test pins that too.

Model.forced_drafts (default on); DSV4.1 off switch TF_DSV41_NO_FORCED_DRAFTS=1.
Test: lanes fire replay, tokens equal on/off and to the fake target, off
gives a9301c957's round counts.
